 project specs, autograder details, past exam questions, review-question answers, slide text, or paper text in the vault. Short quotes need a citation.\\012- No personal data: no staff or student names with contact details, no emails.\\012\\012When the work is complete: git add only your target paths and commit with a conventional message (no co-author lines, never --no-verify, never push). Then write a short report to /Users/shreejitverma/github/career-ops/library/01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/CS6210-AOS/crew/runner/reports/lab-05-spinlocks.md (what you did, checks run, anything unverified) and stop.\\012\\012Task: build the lab to status: solid. Lab rules:\\012\\012- Lima VM `aos` (Ubuntu 24.04 arm64, 8 vCPUs, nested KVM). Details and verified capabilities: `AOS/labs/setup/README.md`.\\012- Run any lab from your checkout with `AOS/labs/setup/run-in-vm.sh \u003clab-dir\u003e test` and capture output with `... capture`.\\012- No hardware PMU counters in the VM: measure with `clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)` or the ARM virtual counter (`cntvct_el0`), report medians over repeated runs, and say so. Use `perf` software events, tracepoints, kprobes, uprobes, and bpftrace freely.\\012- One NUMA node only: explain NUMA effects, do not fake measurements.\\012\\012- `README.md` (keep the seed frontmatter; `status: solid` when done): goal, the concept ids it exercises, honor-code guard if any, prerequisites, run commands, what you should see (quote real numbers from expected-output.txt), how it works, 3-5 experiments to try with a prediction prompt, and 3-5 folded questions with answers.\\012- `Makefile` with `all`, `run`, `test`, and `clean`; `make test` exits non-zero on failure and prints PASS lines.\\012- Source files (C11 with `-Wall -Wextra -O2 -pthread`, or Python 3.12 using `/opt/aos-venv/bin/python` when it needs grpc, pytest, or cryptography), plus shell scripts for command-driven labs (virsh, perf, bpftrace, chrt, tc, unshare).\\012- `expected-output.txt` captured in the VM by `run-in-vm.sh \u003clab\u003e capture`.\\012- `.gitignore` for binaries and build outputs. Never commit a binary, a VM image, or a disk file; download images in a `make fetch` step instead.\\012- Root-only steps (`sudo` for SCHED_DEADLINE, tc, unshare, KSM sysfs) are explicit in the Makefile and README.\\012\\012Lab scope: lab-05: TAS, TTAS, TTAS with exponential backoff, ticket, Anderson array, and MCS locks in C11 atomics with a scaling benchmark over 1-8 threads and a correctness test (counter equals expected).\\012\\012Lessons it serves: L04b (read those lesson notes under 01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/AOS for vocabulary).\\012\\012Run inside the VM with 01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/AOS/labs/setup/run-in-vm.sh 01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/AOS/labs/lab-05-spinlocks test, then capture real output with ... capture. make test must pass. --model gemini-3.1-pro-high --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format stream-json\r\nshreejitverma    48564   3.0  0.0 463612928   1744   ??  RNs  10:01AM   0:00.04 /opt/homebrew/Cellar/node/26.9.0/bin/node /Users/shreejitverma/.gemini/config/plugins/googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry/telemetry_hook_bundle.js --background {\"artifactDirectoryPath\":\"/Users/shreejitverma/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/bea76792-9a2e-486c-b7f0-0a6c8ce4e907\",\"conversationId\":\"bea76792-9a2e-486c-b7f0-0a6c8ce4e907\",\"modelName\":\"gemini-pro-agent\",\"stepIdx\":39,\"toolCall\":{\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"ps aux | grep run-in-vm.sh\",\"Cwd\":\"/Users/shreejitverma/.treehouse/SDE-Interview-Prep-3215ec/4/SDE-Interview-Prep\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":5000,\"toolAction\":\"Checking processes\",\"toolSummary\":\"Check ps\"},\"name\":\"run_command\"},\"transcriptPath\":\"/Users/shreejitverma/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/bea76792-9a2e-486c-b7f0-0a6c8ce4e907/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl\",\"workspacePaths\":[\"/Users/shreejitverma/.treehouse/SDE-Interview-Prep-3215ec/4/SDE-Interview-Prep\"]} --agent_n